      en: "The Tsing Ma Bridge is a suspension bridge in Hong Kong connecting the islands of Tsing Yi and Ma Wan. It opened on 27 April 1997 and is the longest road and rail bridge in the world carrying both types of traffic. The bridge is 41 meters wide with a main span of 1,377 meters. It is part of the Lantau Link, connecting Hong Kong to Chek Lap Kok Airport. Designed by Mott MacDonald, it is considered an engineering marvel. The bridge has two decks: upper for road traffic and lower for railway. It is illuminated at night and offers stunning views.",
