      en: "Hong Kong City Hall is a historic building in Central, opened in 1962, serving as a cultural venue. It comprises a Low Block (with a library, concert hall, and marriage registry) and a High Block (with offices), connected by a covered bridge. The architectural style is modernist. The City Hall was the site of many colonial-era ceremonies, including the swearing-in of governors. It is a Grade II historic building. The marriage registry is one of the most popular venues for weddings in Hong Kong. The City Hall's concert hall has hosted numerous international orchestras. It remains an active community space for exhibitions, performances, and public events.",
